WEBVTT

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.060
Here you go!

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.740
The Pokémon World Championships?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.710
They're tickets to the <i>finals</i>, even!
Awesome!

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.030
I know, right?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:16.780
What's this?

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.960
Satoshi, you don't know?

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.870
There have been plenty of Leagues
and tournaments in other regions,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.930
and they all have
their own Champions...

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:38.310
But the Pokémon World Championships
are where they crown the World Champion.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.890
World Champion?!

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.750
And these tickets are
for the <i>finals!</i>

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.490
So, that means...

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:48.900
We'll get to see the Pokémon battle
that'll decide who's the strongest in the world?!

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.180
Indeed!

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.530
Awesome!

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.950
It will be held in the Galar Region.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:58.660
I'm sure the stadium where the battle takes place
will be filled with surprises!

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.160
I'd like you to go see and
experience it for yourselves!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.700
We will!
Thank you, Director Sakuragi!

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.820
And I'll catch myself plenty of
Pokémon while I'm at it!

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.420
All right! Set off for Galar!

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.180
Let's go to the
Pokémon World Championships!

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:24.770
PocketMonsters

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.190
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.770
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.490
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.360
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.700
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.370
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:44.870
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.130
Each and every one of my memories

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.720
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.640
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:04.390
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.400
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.610
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.950
Let's have a fight!

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.660
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.490
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:25.830
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.500
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.840
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.340
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.470
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.270
I choose you!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:55.280
Dande, the Strongest of All!
Daimax Battle!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.200
How much longer?

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:08.700
The plane has just entered
Galar airspace.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.540
We're almost there!

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.210
Check the power transmission system.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.420
Of course.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.870
Don't worry, everyone.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.930
Please keep your seatbelts fastened.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:26.860
What's up?

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:27.860
Something's coming.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.690
What?

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.000
Nothing's there.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.190
It will be! I can feel it!

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:46.790
Pikachu!

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.440
Cabin lights are back on.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.550
What was that?

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.760
You okay, Pikachu?

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.340
Hey, what did we just see?

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.980
A Pokémon!

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.090
Must be...
It was real impactful!

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.780
I'm getting really excited!

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.700
Seems there's still loads of
mysteries to uncover in Galar!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.060
Yeah!

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.660
I'm getting excited, too!

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.400
We're back in the Galar Region!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.520
It's been a while since you were
in Shoot City, huh?

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.350
So, which way to the stadium?

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.250
It's right in front of us!

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.070
Huh?

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:01.820
Where?

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.800
Look!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.360
Shoot Stadium, Galar Region

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.350
It's massive!
Shoot Stadium, Galar Region

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.790
Shoot Stadium, Galar Region

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.690
Awesome!
It's huge! So awesome!

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:22.050
We'll go catch some Pokémon first!

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.980
Go, let's enter the stadium!

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:27.850
No, I'm going to catch Pok—

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.370
C'mon, hurry!

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.130
Stop pulling me!

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.250
Look at all these people!

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.240
Yeah, there's even more
than I imagined!

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.050
Oh, wow, the brat boy is here.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:52.250
I'd like to say
"Let's get Pikachu!", but...

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:56.220
We have our orders
from Sakaki, meow.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:59.090
Those gigantifying Pokémon
in Galar or whatever...

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.520
Operation Catch 'em!

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.290
And for that purpose, we've been provided
with a new item, too, meow!

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:14.900
Ladies and gentlemen!
The time has come at last!

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:21.180
The world's biggest and best
Pokémon battle fest to crown the world's best!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.800
Its name?
The Pokémon World Championships!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.380
The top eight battlers certified
by the Pokémon Battle Commission,

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:38.810
the Masters Eight, have duked it out
in a fierce tournament.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:43.760
Who will claim the title of
the World Champion?!

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:47.750
Now, then, the finalists
are entering the arena!

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.430
First off...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.930
Contestant Wataru!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.580
It's Wataru!

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.430
Representing our
very own Kanto Region!

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:59.550
One of the Kanto League's Elite Four,
the winner of the Elite Four Cup,

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:05.000
and the winner of the dream showdown,
the Hodomoe City Pokémon World Tournament!

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:10.200
He is also an active member of the Pokémon G-Men,
who takes down his foes with overwhelming force!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.690
His elegant battles using
Dragon-type Pokémon are truly art!

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:20.080
A Pokémon Trainer who prides himself
on his world-class strength! This is Wataru!

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.560
Next up, the other finalist is...

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.030
...Contestant Dande!

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:35.710
Born and raised in Galar, the first time he participated in
the Seed Challenge to determine Galar's strongest,

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:39.510
his overwhelming power
netted him a flawless, undefeated victory!

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:42.410
Ever since then, he has continued to
extend his flawless winning streak,

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.850
and has declared that,
as Champion, he will battle any challenger!

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:52.610
This king of kings effortlessly took down 100 challengers
from all over the world who answered his call!

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:58.530
That is Galar's very own superstar:
The invincible Contestant Dande!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.380
Contestants Wataru and Dande
are standing by on the battlefield.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.000
It's finally time.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:08.760
Yeah.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.280
We will now commence the
Pokémon World Championships finals!

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.260
Both contestants, step forth!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.180
The battle will be a single match.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:23.900
The first to incapacitate
his opponent's Pokémon wins.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.180
Looking at your battles up till now,

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:29.390
I can tell that you are a trainer
of considerable skill.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:33.670
So of course, I figured
you'd make it this far.

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.810
Can you feel it, Wataru?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:39.320
The tense, still air
on the battlefield...

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.060
And the exact opposite from the audience,
cheering and yelling...

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.290
They're both fantastic,
wouldn't you say?

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:49.270
But remember,
the audience is also a bit cruel...

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:51.680
They want nothing more than
to see one of us lose, after all!

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.130
I absolutely love pushing past that fear.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:57.930
I love giving it everything I've got as a trainer
to seize another victory!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.140
It's the greatest feeling in the world,
and I can't get enough of it!

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.640
You think you've won already?

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:07.110
The reason I'm unbeatable is because
I learn from every battle I see or take part in.

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:11.150
I will learn from this battle…
No, this <i>victory</i>, too!

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:16.700
There's no need for words now.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.140
We will battle to determine
who is the stronger of the two of us!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.040
Both contestants,
send out your Pokémon!

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.980
Awesome!
It's an alternate-color Gyarados!

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.980
Contestant Dande sends out
his absolute ace, Lizardon.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:48.840
And Contestant Wataru sends out
the evolved form of the golden Koiking,

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.240
the red Gyarados!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.240
Let the match begin!

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:58.870
Here I come!

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.620
We're going to have
a real champion time!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.530
PocketMonsters

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:06.960
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:11.590
PocketMonsters

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:16.510
Flying
.  Fire  .
Lizardon
PocketMonsters

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.970
Let the match begin!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.260
Lizardon! Flamethrower!

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.770
Gyarados! Counter with
Destroyer Beam!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.760
The Destroyer Beam
overpowered the Flamethrower!

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.160
Dodge!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.430
Gyarados, you're as strong
as I expected!

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.260
Lizardon! Air Slash!

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.310
Stop it, Gyarados!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:16.630
Oh? Despite the recoil from having fired a Destroyer Beam,
Gyarados blocked the Air Slash!

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:19.910
Contestant Wataru's training is
in a league of its own!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:20.980
Flamethrower!

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:26.750
Go!

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.380
Can they dodge this time?

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:29.540
Dragon Dance!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:35.860
Gyarados boosts its attack power and speed
with Dragon Dance!

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.380
But the Flamethrower
hits its mark!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.470
Move in close!
Knock it down with Aqua Tail!

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:55.180
So much power!

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:59.520
I see! Even though the Flamethrower hit Gyarados,
it wasn't very effective.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:04.410
So he figured it was worth getting hit if it meant
increasing his speed and power with Dragon Dance!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.460
It's super effective!

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.380
Lizardon, are you all right?
It's super effective!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.250
Keep up the pressure!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.540
Ice Fang flurry!

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:17.920
Ferocious!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:23.510
Having raised its speed and power,
Gyarados wraps around Lizardon and attacks non-stop!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:26.260
Shake it off, Lizardon!
Fire Spin!

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:34.610
What's this?! Gyarados is
locked in place by Fire Spin!

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:35.930
You're kidding!

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:37.360
What now, Wataru?!

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.610
Gyarados!
Sever it with Aqua Tail!

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:44.370
All right!

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.120
Go! Use Ice Fang!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.330
I was waiting for this!

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.100
Lizardon! Thunder Punch!

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:54.830
What?!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.250
Lizardon used an
Electric move?!

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.840
They were saving it until now!

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:06.680
That's gotta hurt!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.120
Thunder Punch flurry!

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.520
Wataru's going to lose
if this keeps up!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.610
Counter it with a flurry
of Aqua Tails!

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.330
Awesome...

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.880
I'm not finished with this battle.
And I won't let anyone finish it for me!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.110
Of course not.
I was thinking the same thing!

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:43.550
Oh! Is this...?!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.960
Here we go, Gyarados!

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.470
Daimax!

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:08.950
Here comes Daimax Gyarados!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.530
Daimax...

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:14.710
They even use it in battles here in Galar?

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:18.960
This must be what Director Sakuragi meant
when he said “full of surprises”!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.320
That's great!

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.690
Bigger is better, meow!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:30.180
So <i>that's</i> what Sakaki meant
by “gigantifying Pokémon”!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.440
I want one, too!
That Daisocks!

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:34.910
“Daisocks”? Gigantic socks?

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.690
It's “Daimax”, meow.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:41.320
Daimax... That's great.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:45.130
I'll show you what Lizardon
can really do!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.530
It's Kyodaimax time!

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.380
It's Kyodaimax Lizardon!

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.690
Kyodaimax?!

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.230
So cool!

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:17.440
The battle has turned from a regular battle
into an intense Daimax battle!

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.160
Dai Stream!

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.670
The Water-type Daimax move, huh?

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.970
Of course you'd use that move.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.490
Lizardon! Counter with Dai Thunder!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:40.080
Contestant Dande uses
the Electric-type Daimax move!

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:53.430
Aiming for super effective hits
is a surefire way to claim victory!

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.180
Bring them down
with Dai Attack!

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:03.770
Lizardon! Dai Jet!

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.490
They dodged it?!

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.540
Dai Jet hits its mark!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:22.630
I'll show you a <i>true</i> champion time!
Kyodai Hellfire!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.170
Gyarados, use Dai Wall!

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:41.310
Gyarados's Dai Wall
blocked the Kyodai Hellfire!

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.190
Oh, did it, now?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.730
Now, enjoy the climax!

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:07.880
Gyarados!

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:19.720
Gyarados is unable to battle!
As such, the winner is Contestant Dande!

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:23.730
The winner is Contestant Dande!

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.440
Wataru lost...

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.300
Lizardon, well done.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:32.160
Now we're World Champions!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.780
They sure were tough...

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:46.120
Yeah, that Champion Dande
was crazy strong!

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.590
You did well.
Take a nice, long rest.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.390
...It's over.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:09.630
Your Daimax was superb!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:13.390
I once trained
at Galar's Dragon Gym.

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:18.640
And I was influenced by their uniform,
with its rich history,

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.290
and based this outfit off of it.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:24.040
I see. I'm sure they're happy.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.130
It's an odd feeling.

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.540
I'm not angry that I lost.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:31.550
In fact, I feel happy that I witnessed the rise
of a great new World Champion!

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:35.300
Thank you.
That was a magnificent battle!

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:41.900
The World Champion
has been born here today!

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:47.110
Pokémon will respond to a
trainer's strong, upstanding nature.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:50.560
That is how trainers continue to
grow stronger with their Pokémon!

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.520
Like Dande and Lizardon have!

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.590
Then, let me introduce you
once again...

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:05.520
The winner of the Pokémon World Championships!
He who holds the ultimate title of honor!

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:08.360
The World Champion, Dande!

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.570
That's the world's strongest
Pokémon Trainer, huh?

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:17.710
I wanna battle Mr. Dande!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:21.470
Wow, that was fun!

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:24.060
That was quite the spectacle!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:28.060
But we should get back to
catching Pokémon, meow.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.580
A Pokémon I've never seen before!

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.380
It's my turn, meow!

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:40.510
Kajirigame. Biting Pokémon.
Water/Rock type.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.120
Etcetera, etcetera!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.620
"Etcetera, etcetera"...?

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:47.010
But it's a Galar Pokémon, meow!

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:48.870
Then I'm sure it can turn giant!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:49.800
Okay! Let's catch it!

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:52.180
Vending, come on!

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:04.050
Rocket vending secret!

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:08.880
Huh? Just one?

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:13.940
If there's just one, it might be a huge Pokémon,
like the Whaloh from last time!

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.910
All right! Come on!

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.120
The Flower Pokémon...
Madatsubomi?

